  "items": [
    {
      "id": "at://did:plc:565ebob5f6hw33hjdkxty6qj/app.bsky.feed.post/3n2oup53nrs2k",
      "handle": "emollick.bsky.social",
      "display_name": "Ethan Mollick",
      "text": "I see a lot of snarky quote-posts here, but I do not see the \"alternate vision\" Brendan asked for. In a world where LLMs are clearly accelerating discovery in math and theoretical CS—and where 56% of US adults use them weekly—what is the plan? Is it \"wait for this to go away,\" as \"fad\" suggests?",
      "url": "https://bsky.app/profile/emollick.bsky.social/post/3n2oup53nrs2k",
      "posted_at": "2026-11-19T20:06:36.428Z",
      "likes": 176,
      "replies": 22,
      "reposts": 27,
      "score": 7.7,
      "score_parts": {
        "engagement": 2.4,
        "recency": 1,
        "age_hours": 2.3
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "at://did:plc:flxq4uyjfotciovpw3x3fxnu/app.bsky.feed.post/3n2n3vjt7622m",
      "handle": "emollick.bsky.social",
      "display_name": "Ethan Mollick",
      "text": "At its current shipping trend, halving the time between each model release, Google exhausts all the element names on November 24, with a final shipping cadence of 2.5 × 10⁻²⁹ seconds (25 quectoseconds) between Tennessine and their final model, Oganesson.",
      "url": "https://bsky.app/profile/emollick.bsky.social/post/3n2n3vjt7622m",
      "posted_at": "2026-11-19T03:10:07.824Z",
      "likes": 163,
      "replies": 13,
      "reposts": 10,
      "score": 7.3,
      "score_parts": {
        "engagement": 2.3,
        "recency": 0.9,
        "age_hours": 19.2
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "at://did:plc:flxq4uyjfotciovpw3x3fxnu/app.bsky.feed.post/3n2khd3gsqc2z",
      "handle": "emollick.bsky.social",
      "display_name": "Ethan Mollick",
      "text": "That isn't patches because of AI mistakes, by the way, it is patches because AI is discovering security vulnerabilities at an unheard of rate, and if they aren't patched, they may be exploited.",
      "url": "https://bsky.app/profile/emollick.bsky.social/post/3n2khd3gsqc2z",
      "posted_at": "2026-11-18T01:56:34.445Z",
      "likes": 176,
      "replies": 5,
      "reposts": 36,
      "score": 6.9,
      "score_parts": {
        "engagement": 2.3,
        "recency": 0.7,
        "age_hours": 44.5
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "at://did:plc:3igkkqe5nkm66olc4y2syzpy/app.bsky.feed.post/3n2ou2k3tac24",
      "handle": "markriedl.bsky.social",
      "display_name": "Mark Riedl",
      "text": "oh, so organizations that fund effective altruism AI researchers",
      "url": "https://bsky.app/profile/markriedl.bsky.social/post/3n2ou2k3tac24",
      "posted_at": "2026-11-19T19:55:05.421Z",
      "likes": 23,
      "replies": 1,
      "reposts": 3,
      "score": 5.9,
      "score_parts": {
        "engagement": 1.5,
        "recency": 1,
        "age_hours": 2.5
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "at://did:plc:3igkkqe5nkm66olc4y2syzpy/app.bsky.feed.post/3n2oet2en332z",
      "handle": "markriedl.bsky.social",
      "display_name": "Mark Riedl",
      "text": "A lot of Silicon Valley AI labs are Boromir. I can use it for good because it would not possibly corrupt *me*. I say to myself while raking in billions of dollars.",
      "url": "https://bsky.app/profile/markriedl.bsky.social/post/3n2oet2en332z",
      "posted_at": "2026-11-19T15:22:27.910Z",
      "likes": 6,
      "replies": 1,
      "reposts": 0,
      "score": 4.8,
      "score_parts": {
        "engagement": 1,
        "recency": 1,
        "age_hours": 7
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "at://did:plc:3igkkqe5nkm66olc4y2syzpy/app.bsky.feed.post/3n2oet2en322z",
      "handle": "markriedl.bsky.social",
      "display_name": "Mark Riedl",
      "text": "Maybe Silicon Valley AI researchers think they are wizards. How did that work out? Corrupted via Palantir (it's not even a metaphor at this point; Thiel-linked AI funding is everywhere). \n\nGandalf was smart enough not to touch the Ring.",
